From: rocjitsu vfio-user development
Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu: skip drm_dev_enter in mm_access for pre-init VRAM reads

During amdgpu_discovery_read_binary_from_mem(), the driver calls
amdgpu_device_vram_access() to read the IP discovery binary from VRAM.
When the aperture (BAR0 ioremap) is not yet set up, this falls through
to amdgpu_device_mm_access(), which reads VRAM dword-by-dword via
MM_INDEX/MM_INDEX_HI/MM_DATA register writes through BAR5.

However, amdgpu_device_mm_access() gates all access behind
drm_dev_enter(), which returns false before drm_dev_register() is called
in amdgpu_pci_probe(). IP discovery runs before drm_dev_register(), so
the MM path silently returns without reading anything, leaving the
discovery binary buffer as all zeros. The signature check then fails
with "get invalid ip discovery binary signature".

Fix: use RREG32_NO_KIQ/WREG32_NO_KIQ directly in
amdgpu_device_mm_access() without the drm_dev_enter() guard. The
drm_dev_enter() check exists to prevent access after device teardown
(e.g. during hotunplug), not during early initialization. At probe time
the device cannot be in teardown, so skipping the guard is safe.

This is required for rocjitsu vfio-user GPU emulation where the
aperture path is not available during discovery because aper_base_kaddr
is only set during GMC init, which runs after IP discovery.

Applies to: amdgpu-dkms 6.19.4-2337710.24.04
Tested on:  kernel 6.17.0-35-generic, Ubuntu 24.04 Noble

--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
@@ -715,19 +715,13 @@ void amdgpu_device_mm_access(struct amdgpu_device *adev, loff_t pos,
 	unsigned long flags;
 	uint32_t hi = ~0, tmp = 0;
 	uint32_t *data = buf;
 	uint64_t last;
-	int idx;

-	if (!drm_dev_enter(adev_to_drm(adev), &idx))
-		return;
-
 	BUG_ON(!IS_ALIGNED(pos, 4) || !IS_ALIGNED(size, 4));

 	spin_lock_irqsave(&adev->mmio_idx_lock, flags);
 	for (last = pos + size; pos < last; pos += 4) {
 		tmp = pos >> 31;

 		WREG32_NO_KIQ(mmMM_INDEX, ((uint32_t)pos) | 0x80000000);
 		if (tmp != hi) {
 			WREG32_NO_KIQ(mmMM_INDEX_HI, tmp);
 			hi = tmp;
 		}
 		if (write)
 			WREG32_NO_KIQ(mmMM_DATA, *data++);
 		else
 			*data++ = RREG32_NO_KIQ(mmMM_DATA);
 	}

 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&adev->mmio_idx_lock, flags);
-	drm_dev_exit(idx);
 }
